course: dictionary
lesson: 14410
title: Overestimate: thinking too big
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To overestimate something is to think it is bigger, more, or better than it really is. The part over- means too much, so overestimate means to guess too high.
explain: In maths, estimating means making a sensible guess. «I think there are about 50 beans in the jar.» If there are really only 30, your guess is an overestimate, because it is higher than the true answer.
explain: People can overestimate themselves too. «Tom thought he could run ten laps before lunch, but he overestimated his energy.» Do not overestimate what you can do in one day. Plan with care.
fact: Overestimate can be a verb or a noun: you overestimate something, or you make an overestimate.
fact: «Overestimate» means to guess or think that something is bigger than it really is.
fact: «Overestimate» can also mean to think someone or something is better, stronger or more important than they really are.
fact: An overestimate is a guess that is too large.
fact: Rounding up often gives an overestimate, because the answer is pushed higher than the true answer.
exercise: «She overestimated how long the walk would take, so she arrived early.» What does overestimated mean? | Guessed it would take less time than it really would | Walked the wrong way | *Guessed it would take more time than it really would | Forgot the time completely
exercise: The true answer is 48. Sam says 60. Is Sam's answer an overestimate? | No, because 60 is a round number | Yes, because it is exactly right | *Yes, it is higher than the true answer | No, it is lower than the true answer
exercise: Which word in «Her guess was a slight overestimate» is a noun? | a | was | slight | *overestimate
test: «Ben overestimated how many cakes he could bake in an hour.» What does overestimated mean? | Baked the cakes too slowly | Forgot how to bake | Thought he could bake fewer cakes than he really could | *Thought he could bake more cakes than he really could
test: Rounding 37 up to 40 and 48 up to 50 gives 90. Is 90 an overestimate of 85? | No, it is exactly 85 | No, it is lower than 85 | *Yes, it is higher than 85
exam: Which sentence uses overestimate as a noun? | Do not overestimate your speed. | *Her guess of 500 was a big overestimate. | Sam will overestimate the length tomorrow. | We estimate the room holds twenty people.
